<!--
  Commander Battle's Aserai troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame
  only). Same rules as cb_mpclassdivisions_vlandia.xml:
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role): infantry heavy/medium/light, ranged light/heavy, cavalry
    light/heavy, horse archers light. The weight label comes from the multiplier bands (CommanderRoles.WeightBands).
  - The culture's 7 stock class ids are taken over in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true"), so they keep the stock index
    (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex) and every class of the culture is ours. A stock id's role comes only from its hero's
    default_group, so mp_skirmisher_aserai is the medium infantry. The horse archers get a new cb_ id and are appended.
    Never put _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW id: with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class of the file instead
    (MBObjectManager.MergeElements).
  - multiplier: the class's size weight. A formation fields budget x ceil(100 x multiplier) / the average of its role's
    classes, so it only compares within a role.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups. Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon
    slots with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (target Any: commander and troops). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets
    the count. game_mode="all": the server's GameType is CommanderBattle, so stock "Captain" perks would never apply.
  - Culture variance pass (docs/plans/troop-types.md): Aserai are javelin skirmishers on foot and horseback, tabar
    axemen and strong bows, in lighter armour; no pikes, no crossbows. Setups in the plan's order, which
    AssignDefaultClasses relies on (the k-th AI formation of a role fields setup k):
    infantry spear + oval shield, mace or sword + oval shield, tabar (medium and heavy only), skirmisher;
    ranged bow + mace, strong recurve; cavalry lance + adarga, mounted skirmisher; horse archers bow + mace + targe.
  - Two-handed setups clear the shield slot (Item1) with an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn without item (it sets an empty
    element: AlternativeEquipmentEffect.Deserialize) and keep the sidearm in Item2. Skirmishers swap only Item0 for
    jereeds and keep shield and sidearm. Throwing weapons appear only in the skirmisher setups.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
